 "reviewNotes": [
  "The 8 science hours must all come from one area (e.g. all physics); Plotted doesn't check the single-area rule yet.",
  "\"Upper-division coursework outside math/science\" also excludes philosophy logic and C S discrete math courses; Plotted excludes whole engineering and C S subjects to stay safe.",
  "At least 21 upper-division hours and 18 math hours must be taken in residence. (not checked)",
  "Grade of at least C- in each math and science course; 2.00 GPA in those courses. (not checked)",
  "M 408N + M 408S, or M 408K + M 408L, may substitute for M 408C.",
  "The catalog's suggested plan lists M 329F and M 333L twice each; Plotted replaces the second copies (Year 3 Spring, Year 4 Fall) with upper-division math slots."
 ]
}
